WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.600 --> 00:00:06.000
Closed and latched. One rigid bridge holds all three instruments 0.53 mm above their lands. Nothing is clamped.

2
00:00:06.200 --> 00:00:10.400
Press the push tab. One 4 mm thumb press slides a hidden plate and frees the latch pin.

3
00:00:10.600 --> 00:00:15.400
Pinch a lift fin and swing the bridge up. It rests on its 110° stop, so both hands are free. The tab springs back once the pin has cleared.

4
00:00:15.800 --> 00:00:22.600
Lift out any one instrument. Straight up. The other two stay in their saddles, at least 16 mm away.

5
00:00:23.000 --> 00:00:28.000
Lower the bridge to close. Its pin pushes the plate aside on a ramp and the latch re-engages by itself.

6
00:00:28.600 --> 00:00:32.000
Checked on the model, all five requirements pass. Geometry and arithmetic, not a physical test.

